    <item>
      <title>Nikki from Swapnote and Swapdoodle gets illustrated as the first Nintendo illustration of the year!</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/blog/nikki-gets-drawn/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/blog/nikki-gets-drawn/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://external-preview.redd.it/new-smash-blog-post-10-25-2018-todays-item-nikki-assist-v0-NVNlDqs3yqcWs82xXMwq3GNSl2pXofNskp6Ugv7y1-0.jpg?width=1080&amp;amp;crop=smart&amp;amp;auto=webp&amp;amp;s=97d6b1608579c5bb984a711def89dfac8afbdda6&#34; alt=&#34;Nikki&#34;  data-zoomable loading=&#34;lazy&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;First illustration with a Nintendo character? Well&amp;hellip;this is good to be true in many ways!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I am so lucky that I had only one fair share of creating illustrations based off the games that I play in own spare time but the good thing is that this happens at rare times since I mostly focus on my universe. That’s why last night, after listening to the Swapnote soundtrack two or three times, I decided to draw Nikki, who is the software’s mascot, in my own art style.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While I originally intended to draw it my way, it didn’t fit right due to how I draw the eyes for Nikki, so I decided to keep it original and Nintendo-ish in a way so I won’t have to take time on adding some specific details on her.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The artwork will be later published today on Instagram and on Cara. Go check it out by clicking on the links below to see it there!&lt;/p&gt;
